(docs/'CHANGELOG_v070.md').write_text('''# v0.7.0 alpha — Team command center & identities\n\nRelease date: 2026-10-13. Incremental update on v0.6.3.\n\n## Delivered\n- All 216 built-in team identities display national ISO-region emoji flags; clubs also have original procedural inline SVG shields. These are **not** official club trademarks; country symbols may depend on platform fonts.\n- Team plans persist under stable team IDs, including players/formation/captain/set-piece selectors/attack/defense. Imported/exported saves include `teamPlans`. Old saves migrate safely because the field is optional and safe defaults are generated.\n- Unified pre-match setup and paused/halftime command center. Formation supports existing four tactical layouts, and validates a single goalkeeper and unique six starters. Live substitutions preserve clock, score and player fatigue.\n- Three attack styles and three defense styles alter AI positional and decision behaviors. A selected on-field captain provides a small passing quality boost. The designated penalty taker affects penalty accuracy.\n- The extended roster cards retain GK jump/skill stats (regression fixed).\n\n## Incomplete and disclosed\n- Free-kick and corner takers are assigned and saved **only**. Neither foul restarts nor corner kick gameplay exists yet.\n- Club shields are ORIGINAL placeholders, not real crest copies. England uses UK region flag and native emoji fonts differ; an SVG country flag pack remains required for visual consistency.\n- No substitution number/rules; players can swap between bench and pitch without official limits. Career squad management remains separate.\n- AI effects are first-pass behavioral tuning, not human-reviewed match balance or fidelity to Famicom timing.\n''')
(docs/'TEST_REPORT_v070.md').write_text('''# v0.7.0 test report\n\nDate: 2026-10-13.\n\n## Verified automated results\n1. `npm test` — **PASS**: team badge/flag coverage of 216 teams; tactical invalid-input validation; captain, formation, passing/pressing modifiers, changes while paused; inherited 0.6.3 game stat, career, AI, tournament and 151 continental slot simulations.\n2. `npm run qa` — **PASS** in desktop 1440×900 and simulated mobile 844×390 Chromium: command center, team badges, formation, lineup, captain, set-piece roles, attacks, defenses; kickoff with chosen starters; pause then substitute; score/clock persistence in engine tests; saved JSON in mocked storage; existing kits, AI, stats, career, tournament and export flows.\n3. Standalone `play.html` built and exercised by Chromium, without external network dependency.\n4. Screenshot examples: `tests/command_center_desktop.png`, `tests/command_center_mobile.png`, `tests/tactics_pause_desktop.png`, `tests/kits_setup_desktop.png`.\n\n## Not verified\n- Actual file `localStorage` persistence across fresh browser sessions and real disk save-import replay (test environment blocks localhost navigation and `file://`). Browser tests mock storage for same-session assertions.\n- Physical phone/USB/Bluetooth controller, low-end GPU frame rates, browsers other than Chromium, commercial/licensing approvals.\n- Authentic official club crests/flags, current squad accuracy, canonical FIFA/UEFA roster parity and true original Nintendo mechanics.\n- Free-kick/corner gameplay and substitution rules (explicitly backlog).\n\n## Follow-up fixes\nA lost GK Jump field on the new squad page was detected by the existing stats browser regression and restored before release.\n''')
(docs/'IDENTITIES_AND_TACTICS_SPEC_v070.md').write_text('''# Team identity and tactics model\n\n## Identity\n- `src/identity.js`: `countryCode`, `countryFlag`, `crestSVG`, `teamIdentity`; all built-in clubs map to a country and a procedurally generated non-official badge.\n- Exact platform emoji appearance depends on font. To reach true HD-consistent flags in a later milestone, bundle licensed/open SVG geometry in the offline build.\n\n## Tactics schema\nSaved to `legend_teamPlans` by stable `team.id`, never by a changing list index.\n```json\n{"formation":"2-1-2","lineup":[5,3,4,0,1,2],"captain":3,"penalty":4,"freeKick":3,"corner":3,"attack":"Balanced","defence":"Balanced"}\n```\n- Validations: formation known, six unique valid player IDs, index 0 is a goalkeeper, captain active, roles in roster, styles supported.\n- Attacking styles: Balanced, Possession (passing bias), Direct (more vertical movement/shooting).\n- Defending styles: Balanced, High Press (more aggressive chasing), Deep Block (less chasing and more compactness).\n- Designated captain must be an active player; provides small pass coordination bonus.\n- Penalty taker shoot accuracy affects shootout dispersion. Free-kick/corner assignments have no active set-piece engine yet.\n- During paused changes, `GameEngine.applyPlan` preserves match clock, score, compatible fatigue and existing on-field player locations, moving players toward formation homes.\n''')
readme=p/'README.md';s=readme.read_text();s=s.replace('v0.6.3 Alpha — Kits and Agility','v0.7.0 Alpha — Club Identities and Team Tactics')
s=s.replace('## Newly implemented','## Newly implemented in v0.7.0\n\n- 216 graphical team identities: ISO-region emoji flags plus original SVG badges for clubs, including match previews and scoreboard. These are **not official club crests or guaranteed SVG national flags**.\n- Team Command Center in Match Setup and pause/halftime: 6/12 starters, formation, captain, penalty/free-kick/corner takers, attack/defensive instructions, bench swaps. Changes persist by team ID.\n- Attack and defensive tactics affect AI. The captain contributes modestly to passing; the penalty taker affects shootout accuracy. Free-kick and corner takers are *saved metadata only*.\n- Tests: `npm test`, `npm run qa`, `npm run build` (modular + standalone). See `docs/TEST_REPORT_v070.md`.\n\n## Previous updates')
s=s.replace('**Next** remains v0.7.0 team flags/crests, formations, captains, substitution and tactical command center.','**Next** is v0.7.1 stamina/fatigue refinements and substitution limits. The full player creator remains separately staged.')
